														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4381889">
									

<p>My justification is as follows:</p>
<ol>
<li>SCP-4824 contains SCP-4824-1 physically, with a sandstorm wall.</li>
<li>SCP-4824-1 contains SCP-4824 through proper maintenance. SCP-4824 would been effectively neutralized from the passage of time a long time ago if not for SCP-4824-1's geomancy.</li>
</ol>
<p>That said, I understand if people don't think this is sufficient for a Hiemal class (esoteric classes tend to be particularly ridged in their definitions in my experience). However, I personally find it poetic, because to me it implies that SCP-4824-1 effectively and efficiently contains himself.</p>
<p>If you believe that it should be some other object class (ex. Euclid), let me know why.</p>

