			<div class="content" id="post-content-4381941">
									

<blockquote>
<p>It doesn't seem to me that 4824 contains -1 at all, as -1 is stated to be capable of destroying 4824 at will.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I disagree with this logic. Just because SCP-4824 can be easily destroyed by SCP-4824 does not mean that SCP-4824 can't act as a containment unit.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>-1 does not seem to contain 4824 so much as actively maintains its existence. This is not containment, it is perpetuation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I do agree with your logic here. Thinking about it more, it is a jump in logic to view perpetuation as the same as containment.</p>
<p>With this in mind, I'll change the object class to Euclid for now.</p>
<p>Upon closer inspection, is there an established esoteric class SCP that contains itself? Looking at <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/esoteric-classes-complete-list">the guide</a>, I suppose not. I find this surprising for some reason. But I don't care enough to make yet another esoteric class.</p>

