				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4483018&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606380088" alt="TheMightyMcB" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4483018)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;" >TheMightyMcB</a></span> <span class="odate time_1569841472 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Sep 2019 11:04</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4382115">
									

<p>Taking a look due to the disparate rating to comment ratio.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>If SCP-4824-1 becomes unwilling to continue residing near SCP-4824, SCP-4824-1 will be relocated to a temporary containment cell within Site-36, where it will be processed.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Upon a full read, I've noticed that this line never comes to pay off. If that's the case, why dedicate such a comparatively large portion of the containment procedures to it? It's ultimately a nitpick but still something to think about.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4824 is a sandstone obelisk located in the Gobi</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The &quot;Gobi&quot; would not be how a scientific organization refers to the Gobi Desert for the first time. They would say the full name of the geological location, as well as the country that it resides in (since the Gobi is both in China and Mongolia).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>that is precisely 10.42 meters in height and 16.78 meters in diameter</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't think 4 significant digits is necessary here. Feels pedantic.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Visually, SCP-4824-1 is an adult man of good health.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If this guy is Daevite, then he wouldn't appear as an adult man, he would look like an adult Daevite as described by SCP-140. There are visual differences between man and Daeva.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>All attempts to retrieve biological samples from SCP-4824-1 have failed as the samples will transmute into sand when removed.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Comma after &quot;as&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>For this reason, health diagnostics, such as SCP-4824-1's age, cannot be accurately determined. However, crosschecking SCP-4824's interview logs and SCP-4824-1's inscriptions with historical data suggests that it is more than two thousand years in age.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This information (SCP-4824-1 is 2000 years old) could be conveyed much more simply than this, and probably should be. We know he is Daevite and the Daeva have been extinct for thousands of years now.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4824-1 possesses geomancy</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't think this is how the Foundation would express this ability, given that most 'magic' is explained with pseudoscientific terms like thaumaturgy, telekinesis, etc.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Are you sure you wouldn't rather hear the tale of Nadox and the Mekhanite?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I get why -1 would have liked Nadox, what with Nadox being an ostracized Daevite himself, but that tale occurred long after the collapse of the Daevite empire, far away from the Gobi Desert. That tale happened after the Late Bronze Age Collapse, after the fall of the Sarkic Deathless Empire and the disappearance of Prophet Ion. Doesn't really make sense to me how -1 would know what happened to Nadox after he joined Ion, honestly.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Some time ago, I was the only man in line for the throne. I denied the bride chosen by my kingdom… I chose a man instead.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So, a big thing about the Daevite lore according to Metaphysician's Sarkicism stuff is that the Daeva were matriarchal. It's actually pivotal to the origin story of Nadox, as &quot;a Daeva priestess cut off his tongue, sewed shut his mouth, and had him emasculated (The complete removal of the penis and the testicles; an apparently common form of punishment among the matriarchal Daevites.).&quot; As such, I find it really difficult to believe that this guy was a prince who was next in line for the throne, given that the Daeva would prefer a woman's rule. Yes, they would likely punish homosexuality severely, but I doubt the man would even be in the line of succession to begin with.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Dr. Rahal:</strong> You could come with me.</p>
<p><strong>SCP-4824-1:</strong> Seth, I've dreamed about those words. Leaving this desert with you and entering untouched paradises… but such places don't exist.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Okay, this bit here gave me some serious narrative whiplash. We literally <em>just established</em> that -1 was gay like maybe 3 questions ago, and now the doctor is offering to run away with -1 just a few minutes later? I get that they may have interacted previously to learn the language and such, but this just feels like a total stretch to me.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>starting on February 28th, 1994</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why was he given all of this extra time to be around an anomaly that he's on record as being infatuated with? That just seems like asking for trouble.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
Overall, this isn't <em>bad</em> by any stretch, but the dialogue is pretty rocky and your Daevite lore is shoddy, which really takes me out of the piece. Unfortunately, it's a downvote from me.
