			<div class="content" id="post-content-4382660">
									

<p>Well this sucks. I got some mildly glowing reviews before posting but I guess this one still needs some work.</p>
<p>I mostly agree with your criticism, although there are two parts that I'll write a bit about:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>When writing this SCP, I researched Daevite lore through exploring pages tagged with &quot;daevite&quot;. I feel that since the Sarkicism Hub is tied to Daevite lore so heavily, it should be tagged with &quot;daevite&quot;. I'm also not sure how expansion events tie in here (i.e. Daevite history is fluid and can change in an instant. How is this reconciled?).</p>
<p>As for the dates, I chose December 21st 1993 and February 28th 1994 because those are the dates that Don't Ask, Don't Tell was issued and instituted, respectively. I didn't see the two months as a long time because I've always seen The Foundation as bureaucratic and replacements need to be trained (Dr. Rahal is basically one of the only people fluid in the language). I could shorten the time to two weeks, although I find the difference to be arbitrary.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Based on the rating logistics there's a good chance that this SCP will die a slow death. So I think it'll be in my best interest to rewrite this article from scratch and post it in the same place (which I think is allowed).</p>
<p>Is there anyone interested in reviewing such a rewrite? In particular anyone with strengths in historical and/or dialogue centric SCPs? If so, please PM me.</p>

